.TH RUST-ADD-APT-REPOSITORY 1 "March 2026" "rust-add-apt-repository 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rust-add-apt-repository \- add or remove apt repositories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rust-add-apt-repository
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIREPOSITORY\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBrust-add-apt-repository\fR is a command-line tool for adding or removing APT repositories in Debian and Ubuntu systems. It provides a convenient way to manage software sources, including PPAs, Cloud Archives, and standard Debian repositories.
.PP
This is a Rust implementation of the original \fBadd-apt-repository\fR command, designed to be behaviorally compatible while offering improved performance and safety. It can be installed alongside the original Python version.
.PP
The tool automatically handles GPG key management, repository format conversion (one-line and DEB822), and source code repository configuration.
.SH REPOSITORY FORMATS
The command accepts several repository formats:
.TP
.B PPA (Personal Package Archive)
.nf
ppa:user/ppa-name
ppa:user/ppa-name/release
.fi
.IP
Ubuntu PPAs are automatically configured with appropriate keys and repository information. Use \fB--login\fR for private PPAs.
.TP
.B Cloud Archive
.nf
cloud-archive:release
uca:release
.fi
.IP
Ubuntu Cloud Archive repositories (e.g., cloud-archive:bobcat).
.TP
.B URI Format
.nf
--uri http://example.com/repo --dist noble --component main
.fi
.IP
Direct repository specification using URI, distribution, and components.
.TP
.B Sources.list Line
.nf
deb http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu noble main universe
deb-src http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu noble main
.fi
.IP
Full apt sources.list format line. Can be specified with \fB--sourceslist\fR or as a positional argument.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Repository Operations
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-remove
Remove the specified repository instead of adding it. This disables the repository entries and optionally removes associated GPG keys.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-list
List all currently configured repositories from /etc/apt/sources.list and /etc/apt/sources.list.d/. No repository argument is needed.
.SS Repository Specification
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-ppa " " \fIPPA\fR
Specify a PPA to add in the format ppa:user/ppa-name.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-cloud " " \fICLOUD\fR
Specify a Cloud Archive to add (e.g., cloud-archive:bobcat or uca:bobcat).
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-uri " " \fIURI\fR
Specify the repository URI directly (e.g., http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu).
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-sourceslist " " \fILINE\fR
Specify a full sources.list line to add.
.TP
.BR \-\-dist " " \fIDIST\fR
Distribution codename (e.g., noble, jammy). Defaults to current system distribution.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-component " " \fICOMPONENT\fR
Repository component (e.g., main, universe, restricted). Can be specified multiple times. When used without a repository specification, adds/removes the component globally across all repositories.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pocket " " \fIPOCKET\fR
Add or remove a pocket (e.g., updates, security, backports) globally for all repositories. When used without a repository specification, operates globally.
.SS Source Code Repositories
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-enable\-source
Enable source code (deb-src) repositories. Can be used with a repository specification or globally. Use twice (\fB-ss\fR) to add missing deb-src lines when operating globally.
.SS Behavior Control
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Assume yes to all prompts. Non-interactive mode.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-update
Do not run apt-get update after adding or removing a repository.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-login
Login to Launchpad for accessing private PPAs. Requires authentication credentials.
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be done without making any actual changes. Useful for testing commands.
.SS Debugging and Information
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Enable debug mode. Prints detailed information about operations to stderr.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Adding Repositories
.TP
Add a PPA:
.nf
$ sudo rust-add-apt-repository ppa:graphics-drivers/ppa
.fi
.TP
Add a Cloud Archive:
.nf
$ sudo rust-add-apt-repository cloud-archive:bobcat
.fi
.TP
Add a repository using URI:
.nf
$ sudo rust-add-apt-repository --uri http://ppa.launchpad.net/test/ppa/ubuntu \\
                                --dist noble --component main
.fi
.TP
Add a sources.list line:
.nf
$ sudo rust-add-apt-repository \\
  "deb http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu noble multiverse"
.fi
.TP
Add repository with source code:
.nf
$ sudo rust-add-apt-repository -s ppa:graphics-drivers/ppa
.fi
.SS Removing Repositories
.TP
Remove a PPA:
.nf
$ sudo rust-add-apt-repository --remove ppa:graphics-drivers/ppa
.fi
.TP
Remove a repository by URI:
.nf
$ sudo rust-add-apt-repository --remove --uri http://example.com/repo \\
                                --dist noble --component main
.fi
.SS Global Operations
.TP
Enable universe component globally:
.nf
$ sudo rust-add-apt-repository --component universe
.fi
.TP
Remove multiverse component globally:
.nf
$ sudo rust-add-apt-repository --remove --component multiverse
.fi
.TP
Enable updates pocket globally:
.nf
$ sudo rust-add-apt-repository --pocket updates
.fi
.TP
Enable source repositories globally:
.nf
$ sudo rust-add-apt-repository -s
.fi
.TP
Enable all missing deb-src lines:
.nf
$ sudo rust-add-apt-repository -ss
.fi
.SS Listing and Inspection
.TP
List all repositories:
.nf
$ rust-add-apt-repository --list
.fi
.TP
Dry-run to see what would be added:
.nf
$ sudo rust-add-apt-repository --dry-run ppa:test/ppa
.fi
.TP
Debug mode for troubleshooting:
.nf
$ sudo rust-add-apt-repository --debug --dry-run ppa:test/ppa
.fi
.SS Private PPAs
.TP
Add private PPA with authentication:
.nf
$ sudo rust-add-apt-repository --login ppa:user/private-ppa
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/apt/sources.list
Main APT sources file. Modified for global component operations.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/sources.list.d/*.list
Additional repository files in one-line format.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/sources.list.d/*.sources
Additional repository files in DEB822 format.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/*.gpg
GPG keyring files for repository signing keys.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/auth.conf.d/*.conf
Authentication configuration for private repositories.
.TP
.I /usr/share/keyrings/
System keyring directory for distribution-provided keys.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. The operation completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
General error. This includes permission errors, I/O errors, or network failures.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid input. The provided repository specification or command-line arguments are invalid.
.SH NOTES
.SS Permissions
This command must be run with root privileges (using \fBsudo\fR) to modify system APT configuration, except for \fB--list\fR and \fB--help\fR operations.
.SS Component Validation
The tool validates components against a known list of Ubuntu and Debian components (main, universe, restricted, multiverse, contrib, non-free, non-free-firmware). Unknown components generate warnings but do not prevent the operation, allowing for third-party repositories.
.SS DEB822 Format
The tool supports both traditional one-line format and modern DEB822 format. When reading existing repositories, both formats are recognized. New repositories are added in one-line format by default unless \fB--use-deb822\fR is specified (if available in your version).
.SS Global Operations
When \fB--component\fR, \fB--pocket\fR, or \fB--enable-source\fR is used without specifying a repository, the operation applies globally to all existing repositories.
.IP \(bu 2
Component operations modify only /etc/apt/sources.list
.IP \(bu 2
Pocket operations add new entries with the pocket suffix
.IP \(bu 2
Source operations work across all repository files
.SS Repository File Naming
When adding repositories, the tool creates files in /etc/apt/sources.list.d/ with names derived from the repository URI and distribution, replacing special characters with underscores.
.SH COMPATIBILITY
This Rust implementation maintains behavioral compatibility with the original Python \fBadd-apt-repository\fR command. It can be installed alongside the original as \fBrust-add-apt-repository\fR.
.PP
The package name is \fBrust-add-apt-repository\fR to avoid conflicts with the original \fBsoftware-properties-common\fR package.
